  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "This is the easy version of the problem. You only need to compute the score for the given array.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of length NNN, as well as an integer KKK (2≤K≤N2 \\le K \\le N2≤K≤N).\n\nA sequence of indices (i1,i2,…,ir)(i_1, i_2, \\ldots, i_r)(i1​,i2​,…,ir​) is said to be valid if:\n\n\ni1&lt;i2&lt;…&lt;iri_1 \\lt i_2 \\lt \\ldots \\lt i_ri1​&lt;i2​&lt;…&lt;ir​\n\nThat is, the indices are viewed in increasing order.\n\n\nij+1≠ij+1i_j + 1 \\ne i_{j+1}ij​+1=ij+1​ for every 1≤j&lt;r1 \\le j \\lt r1≤j&lt;r\n\nThat is, no two chosen indices are adjacent.\n\n\ni1≤K,ir≥N−K+1i_1 \\le K, i_r \\ge N-K+1i1​≤K,ir​≥N−K+1, and ij+1−ij≤Ki_{j+1} - i_j \\le Kij+1​−ij​≤K for each 1≤j&lt;r1 \\le j \\lt r1≤j&lt;r\n\nIn simpler words, among any contiguous segment of length KKK, at least one index must be chosen.\n\n\nNote that in particular, choosing a single index gives a valid sequence (as long as the chosen index is both ≤K\\le K≤K and ≥N−K+1\\ge N-K+1≥N−K+1).\n\nThe score of a valid sequence of indices (i1,i2,…,ir)(i_1, i_2, \\ldots, i_r)(i1​,i2​,…,ir​) is defined to be\n\nmax⁡(Ai1,Ai2,…,Air)−min⁡(Ai1,Ai2,…,Air)\\max(A_{i_1}, A_{i_2}, \\ldots, A_{i_r}) - \\min(A_{i_1}, A_{i_2}, \\ldots, A_{i_r})max(Ai1​​,Ai2​​,…,Air​​)−min(Ai1​​,Ai2​​,…,Air​​)That is, the score equals the maximum among elements at the chosen indices, minus the minimum among elements at the chosen indices.\n\nGiven the array AAA and parameter KKK, your task is to compute the **maximum** possible score of a valid sequence of indices.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the length of the array and the separation parameter.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum possible score of a valid sequence.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "2≤K≤N2 \\le K \\le N2≤K≤N",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\le A_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
