    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2 2\n9 3\n4 3\n8 1 4 3\n5 2\n5 12 5 9 8",
        "output": "0\n5\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: We aren't allowed to choose adjacent elements; and N=2N = 2N=2 so we can only choose any single element.\nWhen choosing a single element, the maximum equals the minimum so their difference is always 000.\nSo, the answer is 000.\nTest case 222: There are five valid sequences, as follows:\n\n(1,3)(1, 3)(1,3), with a score of max⁡(A1,A3)−min⁡(A1,A3)=8−4=4\\max(A_1, A_3) - \\min(A_1, A_3) = 8 - 4 = 4max(A1​,A3​)−min(A1​,A3​)=8−4=4.\n(1,4)(1, 4)(1,4), with a score of max⁡(A1,A4)−min⁡(A1,A4)=8−3=5\\max(A_1, A_4) - \\min(A_1, A_4) = 8 - 3 = 5max(A1​,A4​)−min(A1​,A4​)=8−3=5.\n(2)(2)(2), with a score of max⁡(A2)−min⁡(A2)=0\\max(A_2) - \\min(A_2) = 0max(A2​)−min(A2​)=0.\n(2,4)(2, 4)(2,4), with a score of max⁡(A2,A4)−min⁡(A2,A4)=3−1=2\\max(A_2, A_4) - \\min(A_2, A_4) = 3 - 1 = 2max(A2​,A4​)−min(A2​,A4​)=3−1=2.\n(3)(3)(3), with a score of max⁡(A3)−min⁡(A3)=0\\max(A_3) - \\min(A_3) = 0max(A3​)−min(A3​)=0.\n\nThe maximum possible score is hence 555, obtained by the index sequence (1,4)(1, 4)(1,4).\nTest case 333: There are only two possible valid sequences: (1,3,5)(1, 3, 5)(1,3,5) and (2,4)(2, 4)(2,4). Their scores are 8−5=38 - 5 = 38−5=3 and 12−9=312 - 9 = 312−9=3 respectively; so the maximum possible score is 333."
      }
    ]
